{"uid":"9b61215c1358c96c","name":"test_run_bounded_reaches_a_grandchild_with_pgrep_unreachable_through_path","fullName":"tests.test_run_bounded_timeout_marker#test_run_bounded_reaches_a_grandchild_with_pgrep_unreachable_through_path","historyId":"ae5cc15183681ce2d0516daec7a6a7ed","time":{"start":1791937879447,"stop":1791937885475,"duration":6028},"description":"Task 009 (M.3, operator steer 008): the descendant walk must reach a\n    two-level-deep descendant (the wrapped command's own child's child) with\n    `pgrep` nowhere on `PATH` at all -- proving the walk goes through\n    `/proc/<pid>/task/<pid>/children`, which needs no external binary, and\n    not through the old `pgrep -P` that silently found nothing on the\n    `procps`-less nightly images (steer 008). If `children_of()` is ever\n    reverted to `pgrep`-only, `pgrep` is unreachable here too, so the\n    grandchild below is never signalled, stays alive holding the pipe open,\n    and this test times out on `communicate()` instead of passing -- the\n    same shape the nightly failure had before commit 545213e.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 009 (M.3, operator steer 008): the descendant walk must reach a<br />\ntwo-level-deep descendant (the wrapped command's own child's child) with<br />\n<code>pgrep</code> nowhere on <code>PATH</code> at all -- proving the walk goes through<br />\n<code>/proc/&lt;pid&gt;/task/&lt;pid&gt;/children</code>, which needs no external binary, and<br />\nnot through the old <code>pgrep -P</code> that silently found nothing on the<br />\n<code>procps</code>-less nightly images (steer 008). If <code>children_of()</code> is ever<br />\nreverted to <code>pgrep</code>-only, <code>pgrep</code> is unreachable here too, so the<br />\ngrandchild below is never signalled, stays alive holding the pipe open,<br />\nand this test times out on <code>communicate()</code> instead of passing -- the<br />\nsame shape the nightly failure had before commit 545213e.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":fal